Run 1: update json@2.2.0. The selector is an exact version. So the range of the variable is =2.2.0, and the header gets 2.2.0, not 2.2.1 (2.2.1 is in the series and is old enough). A new talon.toml is made next to the member file, with json = "=2.2.0". Run 2: update json@^2.2. The selector is a range. The header gets 2.2.1, and the key of talon.toml is replaced by "^2.2". Run 3: update json@2.2.5 names a version that does not exist. The failure (exit 10) names the range of the selector, =2.2.5: an exact version is an anchor range, as R-AD25 writes it. No file changes.
